;; Copy for sessions. Text and inline HSX-compatible markup.
(:title
 ("Recorded sessions.")
:paragraph
 ("List every condition class in a 3.1 MB concatenation of 121 source files, grouped by subsystem, with the defining file. Budget of 32 calls, 400 000 tokens, depth 2. Do not read or search the file directly.")
:paragraph-2
 ("59.6 K tokens in the root conversation. The corpus never enters a prompt.")
:paragraph-3
 ("All 83 condition classes across 14 subsystems, each with its defining file.")
:paragraph-4
 ("Redefine a duration formatter live so durations over 24 hours render as "
  (:code nil "Dd H:MM:SS")
  ", exercise it, commit it. Then break the function on purpose and recover.")
:paragraph-5
 ("The break killed the active process. Autolith wrote crash capsule "
  (:b nil "efa6aa16")
  ", booted the pristine recovery image, restarted from clean committed source with the private commit selected, restored the conversation, and opened a read-only diagnosis turn.")
:paragraph-6
 ("289.0 K tokens, most of it the bounded crash context of the diagnosis turn.")
:paragraph-7
 ("Define a helper, exercise it, persist it as a private image commit, add an agenda entry. Then quit, run "
  (:code nil "autolith resume") ", and ask where we were.")
:paragraph-8
 ("Private image commits " (:b nil "4048480f") " and " (:b nil "9eee3ae4")
  ". The function defined before quitting answers in the next process with no reloading. The agenda entry written in the first session is found, finished, and marked done in the second.")
:paragraph-9
 ("10 min 11 s across two processes. Every persist runs the full validation suite before anything is retained.")
)
